          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(X,F)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with values in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+abelian+groups"} sheaf of abelian groups
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            was originally defined as the value of the right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            functor, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+direct+image"} derived direct image
            functor.
          %p
            But by embedding sheaves with values in abelian groups as special cases of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial sheaves
            into the more general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} ∞-groupoid-valued sheaves
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            and thus the abelian sheaf cohomology into the more general context of the intrinsic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} = Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            defined simply as the set of homotopy classes of maps
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n(X,F) = \pi_0 \mathbf{H}(X,\mathbf{B}^n F)
          %p
            from the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            regarded a (“nonabelian”!) sheaf, to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+object"} Eilenberg-MacLane object
            in degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            The relation of this more conceptual and more general point of view on abelian sheaf cohomology to the original definition was originally clarified by
            %a{:href => "#Brown1973"} Brown 1973
            (whose proof is reproduced below).
          %p
            Brown constructed effectively the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            using a model of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            paralleling the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
            of a sheaf with values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          %p
            The general
            = succeed "-theoreric" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          %h3#more_details_on_this_idea More details on this idea
          %p
            Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
            can be understood as a generalization of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
            from the familiar notion of cohomology of spaces.
          %p
            Which is a simple one: recall that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with coefficients in another space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is nothing but the space of morphisms (continuous maps)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(X,A) := [X,A]
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            – or, in a more restrictive sense traditionally adopted, the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0[X,A]
            of connected path components of this space.
          %p
            Similarly, when considering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
            in their natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theoretic
            home, the cohomology of a complex of sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is nothing but the hom-space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(X,A) = [X,A]
            – where the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            itself is regarded as a special case of a sheaf.
          %p
            One reason this conceptually simple picture is not usually presented is that the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is typically not represented by an
            %em abelian
            complex of sheaves, so that the full simplicity of the story becomes manifest only in general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
          %p
            More precisely, via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            (non-negatively graded)
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
            – which are equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            with values in (non-negatively graded)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} categories of chain complexes
            – can be regarded as special cases of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model category structure
            on the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} (infinity,1)-topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+and+quantity"} generalized spaces
            called
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} topoi
            is that they are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infintiy,1)-categories
            which behave in all structural aspects relevant for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            as the archetypical example
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            does. In particular, as in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} (infinity,1)-topos
            simply coincides with that of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-space"} hom-space
          %p
            In the 1-categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model theoretic models
            these hom-spaces are computed technically by
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,A]
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            an ordinary space computes the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X,A)
            of the complex of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            which is computed by the right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \Gamma(X,-)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section+functor"} global section functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X,-)
          %p
            This, then, is the definition of sheaf cohomology as usually presented: the cohomology of the complex
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \Gamma(X,A)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AsIntrinsicInfinityToposCohomology As intrinsic (∞,1)-topos cohomology
          %p
            Under the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Dold-Kan+correspondence"}> stable
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            we have the following identification of sheaves taking values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            with sheaves taking values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoids"} infinity-groupoids
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectra
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ab
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X, Ch_+(Ab))
                of non-negatively graded
                = succeed "es" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+functor"} homotopically
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
                to the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sAb
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X, sAb)
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
                with values in simplicial abelian groups (i.e.
                = succeed "es" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ab
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X, Ch(Ab))
                of unbounded
                = succeed "es" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Sp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Ab
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X, Sp(Ab))
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+spectrum"} combinatorial spectra
                internal to abelian groups.
          %p
            Let how
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in Sh(X,Ab)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with values in the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            of abelian groups.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^n F \in Sh(X, Ch_+(Ab))
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            with values in abelian groups which is trivial everywhere except in degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            we can regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^n F
            equivalently as a complex of sheaves of abelian groups as well as sheaf with values in
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial sheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{ab}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            of complexes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for the terminal sheaf of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            that corresponds to the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            itself.
          %p Then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n(X,F) \coloneqq \pi_0 H(X,\mathbf{B}^n F)
          %p
            is the degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            class of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with values in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
          %p
            Now write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[X]
            for the free abelianization of the sheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            of integers. Then the above cohomology set, which of course happens to be a cohomology group here, due to the abelianness of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq \pi_0 H_{ab}(\mathbb{Z}[X], \mathbf{B}^n F)
          %p
            which can be regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi n
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq R^n \Gamma(X,F)
          %p
            giving the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section+functor"} global section functor
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            This, finally, is the same group as obtained by choosing any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_F
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaves
            that is
            %span.newWikiWord
              injective
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/injective+complex"} ?
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            regarded as a complex concentrated in degree 0 and then computing the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            group of the complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X,I_F)
            of global sections of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq H_n(\Gamma(X,I_F))
                  \\,.
          %p
            Historically the development of abelian sheaf cohomology was precisely in reverse order to this derivation from the general
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} categorical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Brown1973"}> Brown 1973
                )
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              on (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
              of)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with values in abelian groups, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n F = K(F,n)
              the image of the complex of abelian sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F[n]
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              in degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              in sheaves with values in
              = succeed "es" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi AbSimpGrp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma \circ (-)
                    \\colon
                    Sh(X,Ch_+(Ab)) \to Sh(X, AbSimpGrp)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ≕
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F[n] \mapsto K(F,n) \eqqcolon \mathbf{B}^n F
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then we have the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of cohomologies:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^n(X,F) \simeq H(X, \mathbf{B}^n F)
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  on the left we have ordinary abelian sheaf cohomology defined as the right
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
                  of the global sections functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H^n(X,F) := (R \Gamma_X)(F)
                        \\,;
              %li
                %p
                  on the right we have
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
                  of Kan complex valued
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial sheaves
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi n
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Ho
                          %mrow
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mn ∞
                            %mi Grpd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi n
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H(X, \mathbf{B}^n F) := Ho_{Sh(X,\infty Grpd)}(X,\mathbf{B}^n X)
                        \\,.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              This is the first four steps in the proof of theorem 2 in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Brown1973"} Brown 1973
            %p The proof proceeds along the following four steps, which we describe in more detail below:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Ho
                              %mrow
                                %mi Sh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Ch
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Ab
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Ho
                              %mrow
                                %mi Sh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi Ch
                                  %mo +
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Ab
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Ho
                              %mrow
                                %mi Sh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi AbSimpGrp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Ho
                              %mrow
                                %mi Sh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mn ∞
                                %mi Grpd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    H^n(X,F) &amp; \simeq
                    Ho_{Sh(X,Ch(Ab))}(\mathbb{Z}, F[n])
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Ho_{Sh(X,Ch_+(Ab))}(\mathbb{Z}, F[n])
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Ho_{Sh(X,AbSimpGrp)}(\mathbb{Z}X, K(F,n))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Ho_{Sh(X,\infty Grpd)}(X, K(F,n))
                    \\end{aligned}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  By the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
                  definition of sheaf cohomology,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(X,F)
                  is the cohomology of any complex of sheaves
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi I
                          %mo •
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Ab
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^\bullet \in Sh(X,Ch(Ab))
                  that is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective
                  and weakly equivalent to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F[n]
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi I
                            %mo •
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F[n] \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} I^\bullet
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi I
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H^n(X,F) \simeq H^0(I^\bullet(X))
                        \\,.
                %p
                  On the other hand, by the general formula for hom-sets in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homtotopy categories
                  obtained by localizing at the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} multiplicative system
                  given by
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} CaS
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ho
                          %mrow
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ch
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi colim
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Y
                              %mo •
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                            %mi ℤ
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi I
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Ho_{Sh(X,Ch(Ab))}(\mathbb{Z}, F[n])
                        \\simeq
                        colim_{Y^\bullet \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \mathbb{Z}} Hom_{K(Sh(X,Ab))}(Y, I^\bullet)
                        \\,.
                %p
                  But due to the injectiveness of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi I
                            %mo •
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^\bullet
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} CaS
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mrow
                              %mi K
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Sh
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Ab
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo ,
                          %msup
                            %mi I
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi I
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots \simeq Hom_{K(Sh(X,Ab))}(\mathbb{Z}, I^\bullet) \simeq H^0(I^\bullet(X))
              %li
                %p The second step uses that the inclusion functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ho
                          %mrow
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi Ch
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %msub
                          %mi Ho
                          %mrow
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ch
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Ho_{Sh(X,Ch_+(Ab))} \hookrightarrow Ho_{Sh(X,Ch(Ab))}
                %p
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      first observing that the inclusion
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi S
                            %mo :
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi Ch
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ↪
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ch
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S : Sh(X,Ch_+(Ab)) \hookrightarrow Sh(X, Ch(Ab))
                      of chain complexes concentrated in non-negative degree into all complexes of sheaves is
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
                      and has the obvious
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi T
                            %mo :
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ch
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi Ch
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T : Sh(X,Ch(Ab)) \to Sh(X, Ch_+(Ab))
                      obtained by
                      = succeed "runcating" do
                        %strong t
                  %li
                    %p
                      By inspection, or else by the general properties of
                      = succeed "s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Id
                            %mo →
                            %mi T
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi S
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id \to T \circ S
                      is an
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Id
                            %mo →
                            %mi Ho
                            %mi T
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi Ho
                            %mi S
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id \to Ho T \circ Ho S
                      is an
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  %li
                    %p
                      But by the adjoint functor lemma for homotopical categories,
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Ho
                            %mi S
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho S
                      is also left adjoint to
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Ho
                            %mi T
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho T
                      (since both preserve weak equivalences). So that once again with the general properties of
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"}> adjoint functor
                  s it follows that
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho S
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
              %li
                %p
                  The third step uses that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chain+complex"} normalized chain complex
                  functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi AbSimpGrp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Ab
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X,AbSimpGrp) \to Sh(X, Ch_+(Ab))
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                  that preserves the respective weak equivalences and homotopies.
              %li
                %p
                  The fourth step finally uses that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} forgetful functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi SimpAbGrp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X, SimpAbGrp) \to Sh(X, \infty Grpd)
                  that only remembers the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
                  underlying a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
                  has a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo :
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi AbSimpGrp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} : Sh(X,\infty Grpd) \to Sh(X, AbSimpGrp)
                  (see
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
                  for details), and that preserves weak equivalences (see the discussion at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
                  for more on that).
            %p
          %h3#relation_to_derived_direct_images Relation to derived direct images
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1} \colon Y \to X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+sites"} morphism of sites
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^q f_\ast
              of the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              functor sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} \in Ab(Sh(X_{et}))
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_Y
                    \\mapsto
                    H^q(f^{-1}(U_Y), \mathcal{F})
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right we have the degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} group
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in the given
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Tamme"} Tamme, I (3.7.1), II (1.3.4)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Milne"} Milne, 12.1
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi PSh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∘
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi PSh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi inc
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi L
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ab
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Sh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Ab(PSh(X)) &amp;\stackrel{(-)\circ f^{-1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Ab(PSh(Y))
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{inc}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{L}
                    \\\
                    Ab(Sh(X)) &amp;\stackrel{f_\ast}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Ab(Sh(Y))
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the right vertical morphism is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \circ f^{-1}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              are both
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functors"} exact functors
              it follows that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^\bullet \to \mathcal{F}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+resolution"} injective resolution
              that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi R
                              %mi p
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℱ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo :
                            %mo ≃
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %msup
                              %mi I
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi I
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    R^p f_\ast(\mathcal{F})
                    \&amp; :\simeq
                    H^p( f_\ast I)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = H^p(L I^\bullet(f^{-1}(-)))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = L (H^p(I^\bullet)(f^{-1}(-)))
                    \\end{aligned}
